IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001 (Singapore) -- the leave and pay a working parent has for a child: maternity leave and
-- its pay caps (ss 9(1), (2A), (3), 9A(1), (4)), the Government-paid maternity benefit (ss 9(5A), (6), (6B), 9A(2), (5A)(a)),
-- paternity leave and its pay caps (ss 12H(1), (1A), (3), (6), (6A), (10), 12I(1), (3)), childcare and extended childcare leave
-- (s 12B(1), (1A), (1B), (1C), (2)(a)(iii), (8), (9), (10), (10A), (11), (12), (14), (14B)), unpaid infant care leave (s 12D(1),
-- (1A), (1B), (2)(a), (7), (9)), and the weekly index (s 2(1), First Schedule Part 1 item 1, notes 3A and 5).
--
-- SEAT: the working parent -- an employee who is the mother or the father of the child, asking what leave and pay the Act gives
-- them and what their employer may not do.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 1 April 2025, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CDCSA2001.txt (amendments to Act 46 of 2024 shown).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Part 2 (the Scheme, the child's bank account, trustees, recovery); the self-employed parent (ss 9(4), (4A), (5),
-- 9A(5), 12AB, 12B(16)-(19), 12H(4), 12I(4)); a mother whose child becomes a citizen after birth (ss 9(1A), (1AA), (1B), which turn
-- on Employment Act 1968 s 76 periods outside this deposit) -- answered as `not covered by this encoding`; adoption (ss 12A-12AD);
-- shared parental leave (ss 12DA-12DD, 12E-12G, Second Schedule); the paternity benefit (s 12HA); extra paternity leave (s 12JA);
-- employers' reimbursement (ss 10, 12C, 12CA, 12J); ss 12L-12O, 13-22; the weekly index for an irregular work pattern (First
-- Schedule items 2-3, Parts 2-3); the per-child lifetime caps on childcare leave (s 12B(2)(a)(i), (ii)); the order of taking leave
-- (ss 12B(2)(b), 12D(2)(b)); the reduction of the Government-paid benefit by regulations (s 9A(5A)(b)); s 2(2)'s rules for counting
-- a woman's specified events (taken as a fact).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the working parent,
-- with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001 -- a working parent's leave`

§§ `s 2(1) and First Schedule -- the weekly index`

-- s 2(1) "weekly index": "his or her number of work days per week determined in accordance with the First Schedule".
-- First Schedule Part 1 item 1: where the "Number of work days in a week is the same in every week", the weekly index is that
-- number. Note 3: a day of 5 hours or shorter counts as half a work day. Note 3A: "the maximum number of work days is 6".
-- Note 5: a duration "calculated under this Act as a multiple of the weekly index, if not a whole number of days, is to be rounded
-- down to the nearest half-day or whole day".
-- Gloss: the weekly index is how many days a week I work, at most 6.
GIVEN `my work days in a week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my weekly index` `my work days in a week` MEANS min `my work days in a week` 6

GIVEN days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded down to the nearest half-day` days MEANS (TRUNC (days TIMES 2) 0) DIVIDED BY 2

-- The Act's recurring phrase "N times the employee's weekly index or D days, whichever is the lower". Because note 3A caps the
-- index at 6, N times the index never exceeds 6N, so the "D days" limb (24 for N = 4, 48 for N = 8, 12 for N = 2) never bites.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, wd IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` n `times my weekly index on` wd `work days a week, or` d `days` MEANS
    `rounded down to the nearest half-day` (min (n TIMES `my weekly index` wd) d)

§§ `s 2(1) -- April 2025 Scheme child`

-- s 2(1) "April 2025 Scheme child": "(a) a child born alive and whose mother's confinement in respect of the child occurs on or
-- after 1 April 2025, or occurs before 1 April 2025 but the estimated delivery date for that confinement is on or after that date".
-- Gloss: a child born alive from 1 April 2025, or due from then. A stillborn child is not one.
GIVEN `the day of the confinement` IS A DATE, `the estimated delivery date` IS A DATE, `the child was stillborn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child is an April 2025 Scheme child` IF
        NOT `the child was stillborn`
    AND (   `the day of the confinement` AT LEAST (Date 1 4 2025)
         OR `the estimated delivery date` AT LEAST (Date 1 4 2025))

-- ss 9A(1)(a), 9A(2)(a), 12I(1)(a): the confinement "occurs, or the estimated delivery date for her confinement is, on or after
-- 1 January 2017, or (in the case of a stillborn child) on or after 1 November 2021".
GIVEN `the day of the confinement` IS A DATE, `the estimated delivery date` IS A DATE, `the child was stillborn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the confinement is late enough for this Act` IF
       `the day of the confinement` AT LEAST gate
    OR `the estimated delivery date` AT LEAST gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS IF `the child was stillborn` THEN Date 1 11 2021 ELSE Date 1 1 2017

§§ `ss 9 and 9A -- maternity leave`

-- s 2(1) "confinement": "the delivery of one or more children (including a stillborn child) from one pregnancy".
-- s 2(1) "specified event": a woman's confinement, or certain adoptions; s 2(2) says which earlier events are disregarded when
-- counting first, second, third. The count is taken here as a fact the mother states.
DECLARE `My confinement` HAS
    `the day of my confinement`                                   IS A DATE
    `the estimated delivery date`                                 IS A DATE
    `the child was stillborn`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child was a citizen of Singapore at birth, or would have been` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child became a citizen of Singapore within 12 months of birth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months I had served my employer before the day of my confinement` IS A NUMBER
    `which specified event this confinement is for me`           IS A NUMBER
    `my work days in a week`                                      IS A NUMBER
    `my gross rate of pay for a week`                             IS A NUMBER

-- s 9A(1): a female employee is entitled to absent herself and to payment under s 9(1) if "(a) her confinement ... occurs, or the
-- estimated delivery date ... is, on or after 1 January 2017, or (in the case of a stillborn child) on or after 1 November 2021;
-- (b) a child delivered during her confinement is a citizen of Singapore at the time of the child's birth, or (in the case of a
-- stillborn child) would have been a citizen of Singapore at birth; (c) in the case of a female employee, she has served her
-- employer for a period of at least 3 months before the day of her confinement".
GIVEN c IS A `My confinement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to maternity leave under section 9(1)` c IF
        `the confinement is late enough for this Act` (c's `the day of my confinement`) (c's `the estimated delivery date`) (c's `the child was stillborn`)
    AND c's `the child was a citizen of Singapore at birth, or would have been`
    AND c's `months I had served my employer before the day of my confinement` AT LEAST 3

-- s 9(1): "(a) ... 4 weeks immediately before her confinement; and ... 12 weeks immediately after"; "(b) ... a period of 16 weeks,
-- as agreed to by her and her employer, commencing not earlier than 28 days immediately preceding the day of her confinement and
-- not later than the day of her confinement"; or "(c) ... 8 weeks ... and one or more than one later period ... in aggregate ...
-- equal in duration to 8 times the employee's weekly index or 48 days (whichever is the lower) ... within the period of 12 months
-- commencing on the day of her confinement"; "and for that period of her absence from work, she is entitled to receive payment
-- from her employer at her gross rate of pay".
-- s 9(1A), (1B): a mother whose child is NOT a citizen at birth but becomes one takes leave measured against Employment Act 1968
-- s 76, which is not in this deposit.
DECLARE `My maternity leave` IS ONE OF
    `16 weeks of paid maternity leave under section 9(1)`
    `no maternity leave under this Act`
    `section 9(1A) or (1B) applies, not covered by this encoding`

GIVEN c IS A `My confinement`
GIVETH A `My maternity leave`
`What maternity leave does this Act give me` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Am I entitled to maternity leave under section 9(1)` c
            THEN `16 weeks of paid maternity leave under section 9(1)`
        IF      NOT c's `the child was a citizen of Singapore at birth, or would have been`
            AND c's `the child became a citizen of Singapore within 12 months of birth`
            AND c's `months I had served my employer before the day of my confinement` AT LEAST 3
            AND `the confinement is late enough for this Act` (c's `the day of my confinement`) (c's `the estimated delivery date`) FALSE
            THEN `section 9(1A) or (1B) applies, not covered by this encoding`
        OTHERWISE `no maternity leave under this Act`

-- s 9(1)(c)(ii): the later flexible periods, "8 times the employee's weekly index or 48 days (whichever is the lower)".
GIVEN c IS A `My confinement`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many days of flexible maternity leave may I spread over the 12 months after my confinement` c MEANS
    IF `Am I entitled to maternity leave under section 9(1)` c
    THEN `the lower of` 8 `times my weekly index on` (c's `my work days in a week`) `work days a week, or` 48 `days`
    ELSE 0

§§§ `s 9A(4) -- the most the employer must pay`

-- s 9A(4)(a), first or second specified event: "(i) an amount that does not exceed $10,000 for every period of absence ... equal in
-- duration to 4 times the employee's weekly index or every 24 days, whichever is the lower, of her absence ... after the first
-- 8 weeks of such absence"; "(ii) in any case, an amount that does not exceed a total of $20,000".
-- s 9A(4)(b), third or subsequent: "(i) an amount that does not exceed $10,000 for every period equal in duration to 4 times the
-- employee's weekly index or every 24 days, whichever is the lower, of her absence from work; and (ii) ... a total of $40,000".
-- INFERENCE: a period of 4 times the weekly index is 4 weeks of her work days, so it is paid as 4 weeks of her gross rate of pay;
-- 16 weeks are 4 such periods. The first 8 weeks of a first or second confinement carry no cap in s 9A(4).
GIVEN c IS A `My confinement`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most my employer must pay me for 16 weeks of maternity leave` c MEANS
    IF NOT `Am I entitled to maternity leave under section 9(1)` c
    THEN NOTHING  -- no s 9(1) entitlement: either nothing is owed under s 9(1), or s 9(1A)/(1B) applies, outside this encoding
    ELSE IF c's `which specified event this confinement is for me` AT MOST 2
         THEN JUST ((8 TIMES weekly) PLUS (min 20000 (2 TIMES (min 10000 (4 TIMES weekly)))))
         ELSE JUST (min 40000 (4 TIMES (min 10000 (4 TIMES weekly))))
    WHERE
        weekly MEANS c's `my gross rate of pay for a week`

§§§ `s 9(2A), (3) -- if my employment ends before I take it`

-- s 9(2A): where her employment "is terminated because she resigns before she has exercised, wholly or partly, her entitlement",
-- she forfeits the entitlement "(or the balance of that entitlement)" and the pay for it.
-- s 9(3): "Without affecting section 84 or 84A of the Employment Act 1968", where her employment is terminated "(whether by
-- dismissal, upon the completion of her contract of service, or for any reason other than by resignation)", she forfeits only the
-- later flexible periods (s 9(1)(c)(ii), and the (1A)/(1B) equivalents) and the pay for them.
DECLARE `How my employment ends` IS ONE OF
    `I resign`
    `I am dismissed`
    `my contract of service is completed`
    `it ends for another reason`

DECLARE `What I lose` IS ONE OF
    `all my untaken maternity leave and its pay`
    `only my untaken flexible maternity leave under section 9(1)(c)(ii) and its pay`

GIVEN e IS A `How my employment ends`
GIVETH A `What I lose`
`What untaken maternity leave do I lose when my employment ends` e MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `I resign` THEN `all my untaken maternity leave and its pay`
    OTHERWISE `only my untaken flexible maternity leave under section 9(1)(c)(ii) and its pay`

§§ `ss 9(5A), (6), (6B), 9A(2), (5A) -- the Government-paid maternity benefit`

-- s 9(5A): a woman "who is or was a female employee or a self-employed woman, who delivers a child and satisfies the requirements
-- under section 9A(2), is entitled to claim from the Government -- (a) an amount equivalent to 56 days of her total income during
-- such period before delivery as may be prescribed, where her confinement ... is her first or second specified event; or (b) ...
-- 112 days ... where ... her third or subsequent specified event".
-- s 9A(2): (a) the date gate; (b) the child is a citizen at birth (or would have been), or becomes one within 12 months of birth;
-- (c) "for at least 90 days in the aggregate during the period of 12 months immediately before the day of her confinement, she
-- has been employed by one or more employers, self-employed or both (whether in Singapore or outside Singapore)"; (d) conditions
-- for work outside Singapore (taken here inside the day count the mother states).
-- s 9(6): she is not entitled if "(a) she is also a female employee who is entitled to absent herself from work or to receive
-- payment from her employer under subsection (1), (1A) or (1B)", or "(c)" is entitled under Employment Act 1968 s 76.
-- s 9(6B): (6) does not disqualify her if she would have been entitled "had her employment not been terminated" on completion of
-- her contract of service or for redundancy or reorganisation.
DECLARE `My claim for the Government-paid benefit` HAS
    `my confinement`                                                         IS A `My confinement`
    `days I was employed or self-employed in the 12 months before my confinement` IS A NUMBER
    `I am entitled under section 9(1A) or (1B) or Employment Act section 76` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my employment was ended on completion or for redundancy, and I would otherwise have been entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my total income per day in the prescribed period`                       IS A NUMBER

GIVEN g IS A `My claim for the Government-paid benefit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I claim the Government-paid maternity benefit` g IF
        `the confinement is late enough for this Act` (c's `the day of my confinement`) (c's `the estimated delivery date`) (c's `the child was stillborn`)
    AND (   c's `the child was a citizen of Singapore at birth, or would have been`
         OR c's `the child became a citizen of Singapore within 12 months of birth`)
    AND g's `days I was employed or self-employed in the 12 months before my confinement` AT LEAST 90
    AND (   NOT disqualified
         OR g's `my employment was ended on completion or for redundancy, and I would otherwise have been entitled`)
    WHERE
        c MEANS g's `my confinement`
        disqualified MEANS
                `Am I entitled to maternity leave under section 9(1)` c
             OR g's `I am entitled under section 9(1A) or (1B) or Employment Act section 76`

-- s 9A(5A)(a): the payment "is an amount that does not exceed $10,000 for every 28 days". (b): it "is to be reduced, in the case
-- of a female employee, in accordance with any regulations" -- those regulations are not deposited, so the figure here is the most
-- before any such reduction. The prescribed period for "total income" is also set by regulations; the daily figure is a fact.
GIVEN g IS A `My claim for the Government-paid benefit`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most the Government-paid maternity benefit can be for me` g MEANS
    IF `Can I claim the Government-paid maternity benefit` g
    THEN min (days TIMES g's `my total income per day in the prescribed period`) ((days DIVIDED BY 28) TIMES 10000)
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        days MEANS IF g's `my confinement`'s `which specified event this confinement is for me` AT MOST 2 THEN 56 ELSE 112

§§ `ss 12H and 12I -- paternity leave`

-- s 2(1) "natural father": "includes a person who is identified in the registration of the birth of the child as the father".
DECLARE `My child's birth, as father` HAS
    `the day of the mother's confinement`                          IS A DATE
    `the estimated delivery date`                                  IS A DATE
    `the child was stillborn`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child was a citizen of Singapore at birth, or would have been` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child became a citizen of Singapore within 12 months of birth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the mother and I were married when the child was conceived`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `we married after conception but before the birth`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `we married within 12 months after the birth`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `months I had served my employer before the birth`             IS A NUMBER
    `my work days in a week`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `my gross rate of pay for a week`                              IS A NUMBER

-- s 12I(1): a male employee who is the natural father is entitled to paternity leave and pay if "(a)" the date gate; "(b)" the
-- child is a citizen at birth (or would have been), or becomes one within 12 months of birth; "(c) the child's mother -- (i) is
-- lawfully married to the child's natural father at the time the child is conceived; (ii) becomes lawfully married to the child's
-- natural father after the child is conceived but before the child's birth ...; or (iii) ... becomes lawfully married to the
-- child's natural father within the period of 12 months commencing on the date of the child's birth"; "(d) in the case of a male
-- employee, he has served the employer for a period of at least 3 months preceding the date of the child's birth".
GIVEN f IS A `My child's birth, as father`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to paternity leave` f IF
        `the confinement is late enough for this Act` (f's `the day of the mother's confinement`) (f's `the estimated delivery date`) (f's `the child was stillborn`)
    AND (   f's `the child was a citizen of Singapore at birth, or would have been`
         OR f's `the child became a citizen of Singapore within 12 months of birth`)
    AND (   f's `the mother and I were married when the child was conceived`
         OR f's `we married after conception but before the birth`
         OR f's `we married within 12 months after the birth`)
    AND f's `months I had served my employer before the birth` AT LEAST 3

GIVEN f IS A `My child's birth, as father`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my child is an April 2025 Scheme child` f IF
    `the child is an April 2025 Scheme child` (f's `the day of the mother's confinement`) (f's `the estimated delivery date`) (f's `the child was stillborn`)

-- s 12H(1)(a): "either of the following periods, which must be taken within 16 weeks commencing on the date of the child's birth:
-- (i) in the case of the father of an April 2025 Scheme child -- a period of 4 weeks; (ii) in the case of the father of any other
-- child -- a period of 2 weeks". s 12H(12): for a stillborn child (1)(a)(i) does not apply, so 2 weeks.
GIVEN f IS A `My child's birth, as father`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many weeks of paternity leave do I get in one block` f MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `Am I entitled to paternity leave` f THEN 0
        IF `my child is an April 2025 Scheme child` f THEN 4
        OTHERWISE 2

-- s 12H(1)(b): instead, flexible periods agreed with the employer totalling "(A) in the case of the father of an April 2025
-- Scheme child -- 4 times the employee's weekly index or 24 days, whichever is the lower; or (B) ... any other child -- twice the
-- employee's weekly index or 12 days, whichever is the lower", taken "within 12 months commencing on the date of the child's birth".
GIVEN f IS A `My child's birth, as father`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many days of flexible paternity leave may I take in the 12 months after the birth` f MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `Am I entitled to paternity leave` f THEN 0
        IF `my child is an April 2025 Scheme child` f
            THEN `the lower of` 4 `times my weekly index on` (f's `my work days in a week`) `work days a week, or` 24 `days`
        OTHERWISE `the lower of` 2 `times my weekly index on` (f's `my work days in a week`) `work days a week, or` 12 `days`

-- s 12H(2): the employer "must ... pay the employee ... his gross rate of pay for every day of such leave".
-- s 12I(3): the payment "does not exceed -- (a) $2,500 for every period equal in duration to the male employee's weekly index or
-- every 6 days, whichever is the lower ...; and (b) a total of -- (i) $10,000 for the male employee who is the father of an April
-- 2025 Scheme child; or (ii) $5,000 for ... the father of any other child".
-- INFERENCE: a period of one weekly index is one week of his work days, paid as a week of his gross rate of pay.
GIVEN f IS A `My child's birth, as father`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most my employer must pay me for paternity leave` f MEANS
    min total (`How many weeks of paternity leave do I get in one block` f TIMES (min 2500 (f's `my gross rate of pay for a week`)))
    WHERE
        total MEANS IF `my child is an April 2025 Scheme child` f THEN 10000 ELSE 5000

-- s 12H(1A): the father of an April 2025 Scheme child "must -- (a) give to his employer a notice of at least the prescribed period
-- (or any shorter period agreed between the employee and employer) before absenting himself from work under subsection (1)(a)(i),
-- unless the employee is prevented by any sufficient cause from doing so; and (b) specify in the notice ... the date on which the
-- employee intends to commence". The prescribed period is set by regulations, not deposited.
GIVEN f IS A `My child's birth, as father`, prevented IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give my employer notice before taking my 4-week block` f `, prevented by sufficient cause` prevented IF
        `Am I entitled to paternity leave` f
    AND `my child is an April 2025 Scheme child` f
    AND NOT prevented

-- s 12H(6): "When a male employee absents himself from work in accordance with this section, it is not lawful for his employer to
-- give him a notice of dismissal during his absence or on such a day that the notice will expire during his absence."
GIVEN `the notice was given during my paternity leave` IS A BOOLEAN, `the notice expires during my paternity leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employer's notice of dismissal unlawful` IF
    `the notice was given during my paternity leave` OR `the notice expires during my paternity leave`

§§ `ss 12B and 12D -- childcare leave and unpaid infant care leave`

-- s 12B(21), 12D(10): "qualifying child" means "a child who is a citizen of Singapore"; "child" includes an adopted child, a
-- stepchild and a foster child; "relevant period" means "any period of 12 months as is agreed to by the employee and his or her
-- employer; or ... where there is no such agreement, a calendar year".
-- s 12B(1B), 12D(1A): a male employee is not entitled if he "is the natural father" and "either the male employee or the natural
-- mother ... was lawfully married to another person, or both of them were lawfully married but not to each other, at the time the
-- qualifying child was conceived". s 12B(1C), 12D(1B): if they later marry each other he becomes entitled, from the birth (if they
-- married before it) or from the marriage. The start date is not encoded: a later marriage is taken to restore the entitlement.
GIVEN `I am the natural father and one of us was married to someone else at conception` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mother and I have since married each other` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the natural father bar applies to me` IF
        `I am the natural father and one of us was married to someone else at conception`
    AND NOT `the mother and I have since married each other`

DECLARE `My childcare facts` HAS
    `months I have served my employer`                         IS A NUMBER
    `months I serve my employer during this relevant period`   IS A NUMBER
    `I have a qualifying child below 7 in this relevant period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have a qualifying child aged 7 to 12 in this relevant period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am the natural father and one of us was married to someone else at conception` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the mother and I have since married each other`           IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 12B(1): an employee who "(a) has served an employer for a period of not less than 3 months; and (b) has any child who is below
-- 7 years of age and who is, or who becomes, a qualifying child, at any time during any relevant period" has childcare leave of
-- "(i) 2 days, if the employee serves the employer for a period of less than 5 months during that relevant period; (ii) 3 days
-- ... not less than 5 months but less than 7 months ...; (iii) 4 days ... not less than 7 months but less than 9 months ...;
-- (iv) 5 days ... not less than 9 months but less than 11 months ...; and (v) 6 days, if ... not less than 11 months".
GIVEN k IS A `My childcare facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many days of childcare leave do I have this relevant period` k MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     k's `months I have served my employer` LESS THAN 3
            OR NOT k's `I have a qualifying child below 7 in this relevant period`
            OR `the natural father bar applies to me` (k's `I am the natural father and one of us was married to someone else at conception`) (k's `the mother and I have since married each other`)
            THEN 0
        IF served LESS THAN 5  THEN 2
        IF served LESS THAN 7  THEN 3
        IF served LESS THAN 9  THEN 4
        IF served LESS THAN 11 THEN 5
        OTHERWISE 6
    WHERE
        served MEANS k's `months I serve my employer during this relevant period`

-- s 12B(1A): with "any child who is of or above 7 years of age but below 13 years of age", "2 days of extended childcare leave".
-- s 12B(2)(a)(iii): not "more than a combined total of 6 days of childcare leave and extended childcare leave during any relevant
-- period".
GIVEN k IS A `My childcare facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many days of extended childcare leave do I have this relevant period` k MEANS
    IF     k's `months I have served my employer` LESS THAN 3
        OR NOT k's `I have a qualifying child aged 7 to 12 in this relevant period`
        OR `the natural father bar applies to me` (k's `I am the natural father and one of us was married to someone else at conception`) (k's `the mother and I have since married each other`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE min 2 (6 MINUS `How many days of childcare leave do I have this relevant period` k)

GIVEN k IS A `My childcare facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many days of childcare and extended childcare leave do I have in all this relevant period` k MEANS
    `How many days of childcare leave do I have this relevant period` k PLUS `How many days of extended childcare leave do I have this relevant period` k

-- s 12B(9): the employer "must pay an employee ... the employee's gross rate of pay for every day of such leave that is taken".
-- s 12B(10): "Where an employee has taken 3 days of childcare leave, the amount ... must not exceed $500 for each subsequent day of
-- childcare leave". s 12B(10A): not more than "$500 for each day of extended childcare leave".
-- READING TAKEN: the "3 days" are counted within the relevant period, since the entitlement is given per relevant period.
DECLARE `Kind of childcare leave` IS ONE OF
    `childcare leave`
    `extended childcare leave`

GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of childcare leave`, `which day this is in the relevant period` IS A NUMBER, `my gross rate of pay for a day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most my employer must pay me for this day of leave` kind `, the day numbered` `which day this is in the relevant period` `, my daily pay being` `my gross rate of pay for a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `childcare leave` THEN
        IF `which day this is in the relevant period` AT MOST 3
        THEN `my gross rate of pay for a day`
        ELSE min 500 `my gross rate of pay for a day`
    WHEN `extended childcare leave` THEN min 500 `my gross rate of pay for a day`

-- s 12B(8): an employee who fails to take the leave by the last day of the relevant period "(a) thereupon ceases to be entitled to
-- that leave; and (b) is not entitled to any payment in lieu". s 12B(11): the same if the employment "is terminated (whether by
-- resignation or dismissal, upon the completion of his or her contract of service, or for any other reason)". s 12D(5), (6) say
-- the same of unpaid infant care leave.
GIVEN `the relevant period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN, `my employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I still have this period's untaken childcare or infant care leave` IF
        NOT `the relevant period has ended`
    AND NOT `my employment has ended`

-- Nor is untaken leave ever paid for: s 12B(8)(b), (11)(b) and 12D(5)(b), (6)(b) each say the employee "is not entitled to any
-- payment in lieu of that leave".
GIVEN `the relevant period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN, `my employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be paid in lieu of untaken childcare or infant care leave` IF
    FALSE AND (`the relevant period has ended` OR `my employment has ended`)

DECLARE `My infant care facts` HAS
    `months I have served my employer`                          IS A NUMBER
    `I have a qualifying child below 2 in this relevant period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days of unpaid infant care leave I have already taken for this child` IS A NUMBER
    `I am the natural father and one of us was married to someone else at conception` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the mother and I have since married each other`            IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 12D(1): an employee who "(a) has served an employer for a period of not less than 3 months; and (b) has any child who is below
-- 2 years of age and who is, or who becomes, a qualifying child, at any time during any relevant period" is "entitled to unpaid
-- infant care leave of 12 days for that relevant period". s 12D(2)(a): not "more than 24 days of unpaid infant care leave in
-- respect of any qualifying child". s 12D(9): the leave "counts towards the length of the employee's service" under the
-- Employment Act 1968.
GIVEN i IS A `My infant care facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many days of unpaid infant care leave do I have this relevant period` i MEANS
    IF     i's `months I have served my employer` LESS THAN 3
        OR NOT i's `I have a qualifying child below 2 in this relevant period`
        OR `the natural father bar applies to me` (i's `I am the natural father and one of us was married to someone else at conception`) (i's `the mother and I have since married each other`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE max 0 (min 12 (24 MINUS i's `days of unpaid infant care leave I have already taken for this child`))

§§ `ss 12B(12)-(14B), 12D(7), 12H(6A)-(10) -- what my employer risks`

-- s 12B(12): an employer who "fails, without reasonable cause, to grant childcare leave to an employee who is entitled to and
-- requests for such leave" -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or ... both";
-- (13) the same for extended childcare leave; (14) failing to pay in accordance with s 12B; (14B) a repeat offender: "$10,000"
-- or "12 months". s 12D(7): failing without reasonable cause to grant unpaid infant care leave: $5,000 or 6 months, and "for a
-- subsequent offence" $10,000 or 12 months. s 12H(6A), (7), (8): dismissal notice during paternity leave, failing without
-- reasonable cause to grant paternity leave, failing to pay -- $5,000 or 6 months; (10) a repeat offender, $10,000 or 12 months.
DECLARE `What my employer did` IS ONE OF
    `refused my childcare leave without reasonable cause`
    `refused my extended childcare leave without reasonable cause`
    `failed to pay my childcare leave`
    `refused my unpaid infant care leave without reasonable cause`
    `refused my paternity leave without reasonable cause`
    `failed to pay my paternity leave`
    `gave me notice of dismissal during my paternity leave`

DECLARE `Most my employer can get` HAS
    `fine`               IS A NUMBER
    `months in prison`   IS A NUMBER

GIVEN act IS A `What my employer did`, `my employer has offended in the same way before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Most my employer can get`
`What is the most my employer can be fined or imprisoned for` act `, offended before` `my employer has offended in the same way before` MEANS
    IF `my employer has offended in the same way before`
    THEN `Most my employer can get` WITH
             `fine`             IS 10000
             `months in prison` IS 12
    ELSE `Most my employer can get` WITH
             `fine`             IS 5000
             `months in prison` IS 6
